WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.230
Around the 21st day, this is an embryo seen from the front, here, like this, it's there, with my surface ectoblast here,

2
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:21.230
we see my neural tube inside, the neuropore, the cephalic groove is not closed, and we see what is called the first optical anlage appearing.

3
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.750
And why does it appear? Who can explain it to me now?

4
00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.950
Expansion by support points outwards.

5
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:37.070
Do you remember the main types of communication we have?

6
00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.400
First communication, autocrine. I inform myself directly.

7
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.200
Second type of communication, I inform my neighbor by direct contact.

8
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.550
We are attached to each other, we give each other information of the crine type, that is, liquid.

9
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Third type of communication, telocrine.

10
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.620
At a distance, endocrine.

11
00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:03.590
Neurocrine, it's telecrine. Neurocrine, it's paracrine, in quotes, since it's an axon that comes here.

12
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.120
And then there's another one you don't know, it's called juxtacrine communication.

13
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:16.220
It's that not only is there this information from the ectoblast linked to the genetic, sonetic, HH phenomenon,

14
00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.480
inhibited at the tip of the precordal plate, which means there will be a lateral expansion by

15
00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:24.680
all the phenomena.

16
00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:28.280
that will express themselves and will actually form this.

17
00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.090
It comes out, here.

18
00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:40.970
And we see here that this information from the primary optic vesicle, which is here, you see, here,

19
00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:50.530
you see me like that at the very beginning, you see, and we see these two lateral vesicles appearing, which begin to express themselves,

20
01:50:50.000 --> 01:51:33.207
which are pushing, okay? two lateral vesicles come and come to what is called the part of the epiblast surface. And here, there will be a reaction, what is called a metabolic juxtacrine, which will create a swelling and it will, by reaction of the primitive vesicle on the internal lateral part of my epiblast, there will be a reaction and that it will form, it will engender what is called the primitive optic placode at the beginning I have an epiblastic tissue that appears when the seventh eighth day it is there it is the evolution of this thing at the beginning it will form a plate a neural plate ok because of my notochord which is there will change shape to form a groove then this groove comes to meet To form a tube. And then this part will disappear.

21
01:51:33.207 --> 01:51:36.477
There will just be here what is called the neural crest.

22
01:51:36.477 --> 01:51:40.381
And that, that will form what is called the surface epiblastic tissue.

23
01:51:40.381 --> 01:51:44.014
And so that, that is internal epiblastic tissue.

24
01:51:44.014 --> 01:51:48.252
So the fluid that is here above, it's the same fluid that is here inside.

25
01:51:48.252 --> 01:51:51.262
Okay? What fluid is it? Amniotic.

26
01:51:51.262 --> 01:51:54.822
which will then become, change its name, CSF.

27
01:51:54.822 --> 01:51:57.713
You see that? That's the neural tube, that's it.

28
01:51:57.713 --> 01:52:01.491
And here above, that's what's there, it's the surface epiblast.

29
01:52:01.491 --> 01:52:06.071
It will have these small vesicles that come laterally to swell, swell here.

30
01:52:06.071 --> 01:52:08.471
And then there will be a molecular contact,

31
01:52:08.471 --> 01:52:13.221
which is called a juxtacrine contact, which will change the pupillary tissue.

32
01:52:13.221 --> 01:52:16.681
swell and form what is called the optic placode.

33
01:52:16.681 --> 01:52:20.826
And we see that this optic placode, here, by juxtacrine communication,

34
01:52:20.826 --> 01:52:24.986
becomes a fulcrum. Because what do we feel when we look at this drawing?

35
01:52:24.986 --> 01:52:27.289
You have the impression that it's sinking in.

36
01:52:27.289 --> 01:52:31.155
Okay? In fact, it didn't sink in. What happened then?

37
01:52:31.155 --> 01:52:33.155
It's the outside that's growing.

38
01:52:33.155 --> 01:52:38.577
There is communication and so it becomes a point of support. And so I have an important meeting here.

39
01:52:38.577 --> 01:52:43.484
Between the two, we don't see it here, but there is a cleft called the colobomic cleft.

40
01:52:43.484 --> 01:52:47.544
In which an artery will run, we will see that, the hyaloid artery.

